# .env.example
#
# Copy to .env and fill in real values. NEVER commit .env.
# Nothing in this repository reads a .env file automatically; these are the
# environment variables the scripts in scripts/ expect. Export them in your
# shell, or use a tool of your choice to load them.
#
# IMPORTANT: the website itself needs NO environment variables. It is static
# HTML served by GitHub Pages. Everything below is for maintenance tooling only.
# Normal deployment is `git push origin main`, which needs none of this.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GitHub, used only by scripts/deploy.py
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required only for agents that hold an API token but have no git credentials.
# If you can run `git push`, you do not need any of these.
#
# Create at: GitHub > Settings > Developer settings > Personal access tokens >
#            Fine-grained tokens > Generate new token
#   Resource owner:        your account
#   Repository access:     Only select repositories > luckydomains
#   Repository permissions:
#     Contents ............ Read and write   (required, to commit files)
#     Pages ............... Read and write   (optional, to toggle Pages and the
#                                             custom domain via the API)
#     Metadata ............ Read-only        (added automatically)
#
# Fine-grained tokens expire, 30 days by default. A `401 Bad credentials`
# response means it lapsed. That is expected; generate a new one.
GITHUB_PAT=github_pat_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Repository coordinates. Defaults in the script are kenashe / (unset).
GITHUB_OWNER=kenashe
GITHUB_REPO=luckydomains

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not secrets, documented so nobody goes looking for them
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WEB3FORMS ACCESS KEY
#   The contact form key is NOT stored in an environment variable. It is a
#   public identifier, embedded directly in contact.html as data-access-key,
#   which is how Web3Forms is designed to work. It is safe in a public repo.
#   Rotate it at web3forms.com and edit contact.html.
#
# TLS CERTIFICATE
#   Issued and renewed automatically by GitHub Pages via Let's Encrypt.
#   No key material, no configuration, nothing to store.
#
# DNS CREDENTIALS
#   DNS is managed by hand in the GoDaddy control panel. No API token is used
#   by this project. Record values are documented in DATA_SOURCES.md.
#
# EMAIL
#   Google Workspace, administered through the Google Admin console. This
#   project holds no mail credentials and sends no mail.
